sentences.l:
for indeed anyone, staying a single month away from his own wife,
chafes with his many-yoked ship, whom blasts
wintry hem in, and the sea stirred up;

and we, around a spring, at the sacred altars,
were offering to the immortals complete hecatombs
beneath a fair plane-tree, from where flowed splendid water;

And there were the nestlings of a sparrow, infant children,
on the topmost branch, beneath the leaves crouching,
eight, but the mother was the ninth, who bore the children;

So he spoke, and the Argives shouted greatly, and around, the ships
frightfully rang under the Achaeans shouting,
having approved the speech of divine Odysseus;

But if anyone terribly wishes to go home,
let him touch his own well-benched black ship,
so that before the others he may meet death and doom.

And if you do so, and the Achaeans obey you,
you will know then who of the leaders is base and who of the people,
and who may be good;
